{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update22.json\",\"summary\":\"Registered a fixed experiment for the configuration-recovery question that measures, in a three-voter group, whether a voter that recovers without a configuration still attempts authority. draft/assurance_multi_test.go's new TestAssuranceRecoveredVoterAuthorityAttempt builds a three-voter cluster, commits three commands, restarts node A over its own stores with the replay on in one case and off in the other, records A's tracked configuration, then shuts the other two voters down and samples A's state every 5ms for 1500ms. Two comparisons: the empty-configuration voter must attempt candidacy (expected violated) and the recovered-configuration control must attempt it (expected holds). Local construction feedback showed the empty-config case tracking index 0 with no voters and spending all 267 samples in Follower (never a candidate), while the control tracked index 1 with three voters and was a candidate in 254 of 266 samples; the retained receipt is requested, and its citation in the account of that question is the remaining step if the run allows.\"}"}}
